Now CSS changes. Need ensure mobile HUD hidden on coarse or max 760. Add inside `@media (max-width: 640px)` maybe hide .speed-block/.combo-block? But landscape 844 width with max-height 580 would not be covered by max-width 760? Actually 844 > 760 and pointer coarse, so existing touch display rule applies. Add a new media query for coarse pointer. Could append:

```
@media (pointer: coarse) {
  body[data-state='playing'] .hud-bottom { display: none; }
  .touch-btn { background: ...}
}
```
But `body[data-state='playing'] .hud-bottom` display flex by default; hiding only during playing is fine because HUD only visible then. At max-width 760 on desktop testing with mouse, touch controls display even though pointer fine; then HUD bottom would still show and overlap. So include `(pointer: coarse), (max-width: 760px)` in the media query. Add near existing rule.

Also maybe `touch-btn` stronger. Let's edit.

